Curators Comments:
Bibliography:
S. Parpola, ‘Letters from Assyrian Scholars to the Kings Esarhaddon and Ashurbanipal, 2: Commentary and Appendices’ (Alte Orient Altes Testament 5/2). (Kevelaer/Neukirchen-Vluyn, 1983), 66, no. 61;
S. Parpola, ‘Letters from Assyrian and Babylonian Scholars’ (State Archives of Assyria 10). (Helsinki, 1993), 57, no. 75.

The docket is evidence for the increasing use of the Aramaic language and script as an alternative to Assyrian cuneiform during the last decades of the Assyrian empire.
Bibliography:
F. M. Fales, ‘Aramaic Epigraphs on Clay Tbalets of the Neo-Assyrian Period’ (Studi Semitici, nuova serie, 2). (Rome, 1986), 157-61, no. 13;
S. J. Lieberman, ‘The Aramaic argillary script in the seventh century’. ‘Bulletin of the American Schools of Oriental Research’ (Cambridge, Mass., 1968), 25-30;
S. Herbordt, ‘Neuassyrische Glyptik des 8.-7 Jh. V. Chr.’ (State Archives of Assyria Studies 1), (Helsinki, 1992), 249, Ninive 186.
